      "updated": 1787028253881,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "* requestAnimationFrame does not make the network faster. It\nis purely a UI scheduling optimization: you can receive 50–100\nchunks per second but only render at a browser-friendly cadence.\n\n* requestAnimationFrame is useful when the tab is visible, but\nbrowsers heavily throttle it in background tabs. That’s usually\nfine because you still accumulate the complete response in\npendingTextRef; when rendering resumes, the UI jumps to the\nlatest text instead of losing chunks.\n\n* EventSource can receive events as fast as the server produces\nthem, while requestAnimationFrame coalesces multiple token\nupdates into one React render aligned with the browser paint\ncycle.\n\n---------------------------------------------\n\nLLM\n │\n │ token chunks\n ▼\nBackend\n │\n │ SSE\n ▼\nEventSource\n │\n │ text.delta\n ▼\npendingTextRef\n │\n │ accumulate immediately\n ▼\nrequestAnimationFrame\n │\n │ at most once per browser frame\n ▼\nsetText()\n │\n ▼\nReact render",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "* requestAnimationFrame does not make the network faster. It is purely a UI scheduling optimization: you can receive 50–100 chunks per second but only render at a browser-friendly cadence.\n\n* requestAnimationFrame is useful when the tab is visible, but browsers heavily throttle it in background tabs. That’s usually fine because you still accumulate the complete response in pendingTextRef; when rendering resumes, the UI jumps to the latest text instead of losing chunks.\n\n* EventSource can receive events as fast as the server produces them, while requestAnimationFrame coalesces multiple token updates into one React render aligned with the browser paint cycle.\n\n---------------------------------------------\n\nLLM\n │\n │ token chunks\n ▼\nBackend\n │\n │ SSE\n ▼\nEventSource\n │\n │ text.delta\n ▼\npendingTextRef\n │\n │ accumulate immediately\n ▼\nrequestAnimationFrame\n │\n │ at most once per browser frame\n ▼\nsetText()\n │\n ▼\nReact render",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
